      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DOREEN KEEPING (2) was prominent early from the tricky draw and did a fair job to be beaten 5.5 lengths into second (16.20) at this track in a Grade 5/6 over 275m. Yet to win out of this box but has been in the placings six times from 11 starts. Key chance in this line up. QUEEN POTATO (1) hit the ground running last time with a fast early split and never headed, leading throughout to win by a neck (16.07) over 275m at this track. Goes well out of this box with a win and two minor placings. Can make it two on the bounce. CIDER (4) was below best at his last couple, the latest finishing seventh at Mandurah, but was among the placings at Mandurah three back. Key player on best and worth another try. MISS SWITZERLAND (7) with some luck can improve on an unplaced run last time here.",
